Implement user story SKY-002-b: Test suite for SkyscannerClient

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with vitest tests covering URL/header construction, response parsing, error handling, constructor validation, and mock mode behavior — all using mocked fetch with no real network calls.

## Acceptance Criteria
- client.test.ts uses vitest with mocked global fetch (vi.stubGlobal or equivalent) and afterEach restoration — no real network calls in any test
- Tests verify correct RapidAPI URL and header construction, and successful response parsed into FlightResult[]
- Tests verify HTTP 4xx/5xx rejection with status code in error message, and malformed response body rejects with parse/validation error
- Tests verify missing/empty API key constructor error (including empty string apiKey and empty RAPIDAPI_KEY env var)
- Tests verify mock mode: MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' returns fixture without fetch invocation; non-'true' values perform real fetch; tsc --noEmit exits 0 and vitest run exits 0


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- Class SkyscannerClient exported from module
- Constructor signature: constructor(options: { apiKey?: string } = {})
- Constructor throws 'API key cannot be empty string' when options.apiKey is empty string
- Constructor throws 'Missing API key: provide apiKey option or set RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable' when no apiKey provided and RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is undefined or empty
- Constructor accepts RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable when options.apiKey not provided and env var is non-empty
- Method searchFlights signature: async searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- SearchParams interface: { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number }
- FlightResult interface: { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number }
- searchFlights checks process.env.MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true' for mock mode
- Mock mode returns MOCK_FLIGHTS array directly without calling fetch
- Non-mock mode constructs URL: https://skyscanner-api.p.rapidapi.com/v3/flights/search
- Query params set: 'origin', 'destination', 'date', and optional 'adults'
- HTTP headers: 'X-RapidAPI-Key' and 'X-RapidAPI-Host': 'skyscanner-api.p.rapidapi.com'
- HTTP method: GET
- On !response.ok: throws 'HTTP error ${response.status}: ${response.statusText}'
- On JSON parse failure: throws 'Failed to parse response JSON'
- On invalid response format: throws 'Invalid response format: missing required fields'
- isValidFlightResponse validates: Array.isArray(data) and each item has price (number), currency (string), airline (string), departure (string), arrival (string), duration (number), stops (number)
- MOCK_FLIGHTS fixture contains 3 flights with all required FlightResult fields

## Mock Strategy
